      <h1 id="creating-dns-records-on-aws" class="group scroll-mt-20">Creating DNS records on AWS<a href="#creating-dns-records-on-aws" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="_abstract">To create DNS records on AWS and AWS GovCloud, use the External DNS Operator. The Operator manages external name resolution for your cluster services directly through the Operator.</p>
      <Alert variant="info" class="my-4">
        <AlertTitle>Important</AlertTitle>
        <AlertDescription>
          <p>Usage of External DNS Operator on an STS-enabled cluster that runs in AWS Government (AWS GovCloud) regions is not supported.</p>
